      "text_raw": "This layout is shown that\nmost input stage devices are\nquite big. Indeed, they are\nused in weak inversion,\nwhich leads to large W/L\nratios.\nThe specifications are\nadded as well. They show a\nFOM of about 320 MHzpF/\nmA, which is very reason-\nable indeed. This shows that\na replica input stage does\nnot add all that much to the\npower consumption. After\nall, the current consumption\nin the first stage of a\ntwo-stage opamp is always small. Doubling it is not going to make a big difference in total\npower consumption.",
      "text": "This layout is shown that most input stage devices are quite big. Indeed, they are used in weak inversion, which leads to large W/L ratios. The specifications are added as well. They show a FOM of about 320 MHzpF/ mA, which is very reasonable indeed. This shows that a replica input stage does not add all that much to the power consumption. After all, the current consumption in the first stage of a two-stage opamp is always small. Doubling it is not going to make a big difference in total power consumption."
